<%
  /*
   * "Powered & Secured By" — IndusDefender and IndusNetwork.
   *
   * The two marks, the label and the order of the sign-in page at
   * marthoma.online, in this directory's own palette rather than that site's
   * navy and gold: the plate is `--vellum` over `--rule`, the same pairing
   * the rest of the application uses for a panel, so it reads as part of the
   * page instead of a window cut into it.
   *
   * "Protect. Prevent. Prevail." is set in text here. It is baked into the
   * bottom of the supplied shield in near-white, which was right on a navy
   * panel and would be invisible on this one, so the artwork is cropped free
   * of it and the words are typed — which also lets "Prevail." keep its
   * accent, in the palette's own gilt.
   *
   * The wordmark is set in Fraunces, which the directory already loads for
   * its own headings, rather than in a second serif carried for this plate
   * alone.
   *
   * The network mark is the current banner — the wordmark reversed out of its
   * own navy-to-maroon ground, not the older dark-on-transparent lock-up. It
   * therefore needs no chip under it: it is already a tile, and a light card
   * behind a dark one would only be a second border. It keeps the corner
   * radius and takes the same lift the shield has, so the two marks sit at
   * the same height off the plate.
   */
%>
<div class="indus-badge">
  <span class="plabel">Powered &amp; Secured By</span>

  <div class="logos">
    <span class="owlwrap">
      <span class="owlname">Indus<span class="def">Defender</span></span>
      <img class="owl" src="<%= base %>/images/indus-defender.png"
           alt="IndusDefender" width="145" height="176">
      <span class="owltag">Protect. Prevent. <span class="last">Prevail.</span></span>
    </span>

    <span class="divider"></span>

    <span class="induschip">
      <img class="indus" src="<%= base %>/images/indus-network-banner.jpg"
           alt="INDUSNETWORK.ORG — Collaboration Creates Success."
           width="520" height="235" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    </span>
  </div>
</div>
